# Play Store positioning (India)

This product is **record-keeping software for a pawn-broking shop**: shop ledger
plus a customer receipt viewer. Money moves at the counter. Nobody applies for
credit inside the app.

Google Play classifies India financial apps from **store listing text and
screenshots first**. Wrong wording pulls the app into personal-loan / DLA review
that a state-licensed pawnbroker usually cannot satisfy. A false Financial
features declaration becomes false the moment the binary collects repayments
online or lets customers apply for credit.

## Store listing — forbidden words and framing

Do **not** use these in the **store title**, **short description**, **full
description**, or **screenshot captions / on-image text**:

- loan / gold loan
- girvi finance
- credit
- EMI
- interest rate

Describe the app as **record-keeping for a pawn-broking shop** (pledge records,
receipts, shop ledger, customer receipt viewer). Prefer: pledge, pawn shop,
record keeping, receipt, ledger, shop book.

Never: "get a loan", "apply", "instant cash", credit offers, or marketing that
implies in-app lending.

## Product hard stops (keep the declaration true)

- **No in-app repayment collection** — no UPI, Razorpay, cards, wallets, or any
  payment gateway for collecting principal / dues inside the app.
- **No customer "apply for loan" / self-service pledge application flow.**
  Customers are read-only: view their own receipts / pledge records. Shop staff
  create records at the counter.
- Do not add credit offers, loan marketplaces, or disbursement marketing on
  customer surfaces.

Internal SQL/domain terms (`loans` table, interest engine) may remain in code
and shop-only UI. That does **not** license those words on the Play listing or
on screenshots submitted to Play Console.

## When editing copy or features

1. Play Console assets and any marketing screenshot → follow the banned-word
   list above.
2. New customer features → receipt/viewer only; refuse apply / pay-online work.
3. Financial features declaration → stay honest; do not ship payment collection
   or apply-for-credit without an explicit product decision that accepts
   reclassification as a lending app.
